[GENERAL]
MapName=KOKUBO SOSHO
Briefing=TODO
Briefing_LAMBERT=LAMBERT - State Department has lost contact with all of the US Officers who work at the Kokubo Sosho with the Japanese Self Defense Force. It looks like the SDF have taken them prisoner and they're refusing to answer our calls. In typical fashion, the Japanese are circling their wagons... either they're afraid to admit they've lost control of Otomo, or they're actually sanctioning him. If that's the case we'll have to come clean with North Korea, which will spark a massive war in Asia. If not... we need to find out what our officers know and figure out what to do about Otomo before North Korea finds out what's going on.
Briefing_GRIMSDOTTIR=GRIMSDOTTIR - Sam, even if the Japanese government does not sanction him, Otomo still clearly has the capacity to strike. If he is still in control of the Information arm of the SDF, you'll need to deal with him very carefully. There is no telling what kind of havoc he could unleash.
Briefing_REDDING=REDDING - Last contact we had with any US personnel in the Kokubo Sosho was a fragment of a phonecall from Major Harper, a logistics advisor to G-SDF. Form the sounds of the call, the room he was in was raided by Japanese troops and he was taken prisoner. It doesn't sound like anyone has been killed... and if there is any hope of maintaining peaceful relations with the Japanese, you're going to have to keep it that way.

